From 063b9db399351ea97eddaf44dd49b951e00a72e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:36:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] apply-image-verdicts: keep the image descriptions drafted in
 other languages

image-verdicts.json holds a verdict's English description; for most
documents the Arabic, Chinese, French, Russian and Spanish drafts were
written into the sidecars afterwards. Rebuilding a sidecar from the
verdicts alone dropped them: on every re-ingest (pdf-images.py rewrites
images.json, the staging arm re-applied English only) and on every bare
run of this script (the who-iris re-ingest pilot, 2026-11-14, lost them
on 15 images of two entries, and a bare run stripped 10 other entries).

A verdict's drafts now keep the narratives already held in the
languages the verdict does not supply, when the held narrative in the
verdict's own language is the same text. A changed English description
drops them, since they translate something else. A staged re-ingest
takes them from the entry as filed in the library. Over who-iris's 272
judged sidecars, none loses a narrative.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
